Ladybird evaluates the font-relative size queries below a container
again only when the font the container holds after an update differs,
by value, from the one it held before. Blink compares the old and new
fonts with ValuesEquivalent() in ContainerQueryEvaluator::
ApplyScrollStateAndStyleChanges(), WebKit compares the new style with
the renderer’s existing one through fontCascadeEqual() in its
styleChangeAffectsRelativeUnits(), and Gecko’s finish_restyle() raises
RESTYLE_IF_AFFECTED_BY_WM_OR_ANCESTOR_FONT only when the font size or
line height changed. All three compare styles that include the
animated values already, so none of them sees a font change in the
base style of a running transition.
